WHAT MAKES A PROBLEM GREEDY?
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Greedy works when: making the locally best choice at each step
leads to the globally best answer.

Before coding, ask yourself:
"If I always pick the best option right now,
can a future choice ever make me regret this decision?"

If YES → greedy fails, use DP instead.
If NO → greedy is safe, and it will be O(n) or O(n log n).

The hardest skill in greedy is proving your choice is safe.
Ask: "What is the WORST thing that could happen if I pick this?"
If the answer is "nothing — it can only help or stay neutral", greedy works.

