PATTERN 3 — RUNNING GREEDY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Process elements left to right, track a running value
→ Make a greedy decision at each step based on that running value
→ Problems that "reset" when a condition is violated

EXAMPLE — Gas Station
https://leetcode.com/problems/gas-station

If total gas >= total cost, a solution always exists.
If tank goes negative from some start point → that start (and every
point between) cannot be the answer. Reset and try starting fresh.
int canCompleteCircuit(vector<int>& gas, vector<int>& cost) {
    int total = 0, tank = 0, start = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < gas.size(); i++) {
        int gain = gas[i] - cost[i];
        total += gain;
        tank  += gain;
        if (tank < 0) { start = i + 1; tank = 0; }
    }
    return total >= 0 ? start : -1;
}
EXAMPLE — Partition Labels
https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-labels

Each partition must extend to include the LAST occurrence of
every character seen so far. When current index == farthest → end partition.
vector<int> partitionLabels(string s) {
    int last[26] = {};
    for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) last[s[i]-'a'] = i;

    vector<int> res;
    int start = 0, end = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {
        end = max(end, last[s[i]-'a']);
        if (i == end) { res.push_back(end - start + 1); start = i + 1; }
    }
    return res;
}
EXAMPLE — Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock II (multiple transactions)
https://leetcode.com/problems/best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock-ii

Collect every upward price movement. Sum all positive day-to-day gains.
int maxProfit(vector<int>& prices) {
    int profit = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i < prices.size(); i++)
        profit += max(0, prices[i] - prices[i-1]);
    return profit;
}
