HOW TO IDENTIFY WHICH PATTERN — DECISION GUIDE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Read the problem. Ask these questions in order:

Does "best available right now" change dynamically as you process?
→ YES → Pattern 4 (Heap Greedy)

Does it involve time intervals, ranges, or reachability?
→ YES → Pattern 1 (Interval Greedy — sort by END time)

Does it involve a running total that resets or extends?
→ YES → Pattern 3 (Running Greedy — scan left to right)

Can you solve it by sorting in a specific order and assigning?
→ YES → Pattern 2 (Sort + Assign — think hard about WHAT to sort by)

GREEDY VS DP:
Coin Change → greedy fails (picking largest coin can block valid completion).
Jump Game → greedy works (extending farthest never blocks a better option).
The test: does the current choice ever prevent a better future choice?
YES → DP. NO → greedy.

